This license covers the source code, build scripts and original assets of
Dan's Bridges (the "Mod"), but not the third-party content described in
section 4. The Mod is published at
https://github.com/WinDanesz/Bridges. "Official Releases" are the
compiled builds of the Mod published by the Author on the Mod's official
project pages. The "Author" is WinDanesz.


1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

  a) Read, study, build and run the source code.

  b) Fork the repository and publish your fork's source code, for example
     on GitHub, as long as this license file stays with it unchanged.

  c) Modify the Mod and build it for your own use, including on private
     servers you run and in modpacks that you do not publish.

  d) Share builds of a modified Mod privately with a small group of people
     for testing, such as the players of your server, as long as they are
     not offered to the public.

  e) Submit changes to the Mod, such as pull requests, issues with patches
     or other code (see section 3).

  f) Include unmodified Official Releases in a modpack, including a public
     one, or point to them from it.

  g) Use small portions of the code, such as single methods or techniques,
     in your own distinct project, with credit to the Author and a link to
     this repository, as long as that project is not a substitute for the
     Mod or for one of its features as a whole.

  h) Let an automated build service, such as GitHub Actions, build your
     fork or your pull request and keep the builds as temporary build
     artifacts of that service, for testing and review.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

  a) Publish or distribute, publicly, any compiled build (such as a .jar
     file) of a modified version of the Mod, or of a fork of it. This
     covers mod hosting sites (including CurseForge, Modrinth and
     Planet Minecraft, etc.), launchers, mod portals, download sites, release
     pages, and any other place where the
     public can get it. It also covers public modpacks that contain such
     a build. The only exception is the build artifacts in continuous integration services, such as GitHub Actions, that are used for testing and review.

  b) Re-upload Official Releases on their own, outside a modpack, to any
     site or service.

  c) Publish the Mod, a fork of it, or a substantial part of it, under a
     different name or as your own project, whether as a build or as a
     project page on a mod hosting site.

  d) Sell the Mod or a fork of it, or put access to it behind a payment.

  e) Remove or change copyright notices, credits or this license.

If you want to do any of the above, ask the Author. Permission is only
given in writing, by the Author, and only for what it names.


